&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Robotics and Mechatronics Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;(Senior) Systems and Safety Engineer (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;, who will own system-level engineering and functional safety for our robot. You&#39;ll decide whether a design is safe enough to ship, since missing a hazard here risks real injury.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Elicit, write, review, and manage system, subsystem, and safety requirements with full traceability, keeping requirements, architecture, implementation, and verification artifacts linked across the system lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Define, maintain, and review system and subsystem architecture, including interfaces, functional decomposition, and requirements allocation across the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hazard &amp;amp; Safety Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform hazard analysis, risk assessment, and failure analysis (FMEA, FMEDA, fault tree analysis where applicable), and define the safety concepts, safety functions, and fault reaction strategies that follow from it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certification Work Products:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain the safety and systems engineering work products required for certification, including the safety plan, verification and validation plan, and system architecture documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Team Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Work across hardware, software, mechanical, and test teams to keep the system coherent, safety-compliant, and fully covered by traceable requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Robotics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems &amp;amp; Safety Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience applying systems engineering and functional safety practices to complex electromechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Failure Analysis Techniques:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience conducting FMEA, FMEDA, or fault tree analysis to identify and assess system hazards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of machinery and robot safety standards, including ISO 10218, ISO 13849, IEC 61508, IEC 60204, IEC 61800, and IEC 61010.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schematics &amp;amp; Firmware Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to read and understand electronic schematics and related firmware at a system level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A dynamic high-tech company, combined with financial soundness and world-class investors.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Join an interdisciplinary, international team with 60+ different nationalities in a collaborative work environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lots of development opportunities as we continue to grow.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Challenging tasks and impactful projects alongside experts that enable professional and personal growth.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Corporate Benefits Program covering health, mobility, and learning for 100€ net per month.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
